WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.060
Set up WhatsApp safely, and lock your account.

2
00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:08.020
This is the video for module one of WhatsApp for Communication and Business.

3
00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:17.220
Your WhatsApp account is tied to one phone number. That number becomes your identity, so choose a line you plan to keep for years.

4
00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:20.480
First, install the genuine app, and nothing else.

5
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:27.510
Next, you will see why the six-digit code that comes by SMS must never leave your hands.

6
00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:33.860
Then you will switch on two-step verification, the most important setting in WhatsApp.

7
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:39.690
And you will back up your chats, so a lost phone does not take your customers with it.

8
00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:49.950
Only install WhatsApp from the Google Play Store on Android, or the App Store on iPhone. Check that the developer is WhatsApp LLC.

9
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.750
Keep it updated for security fixes.

10
00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:05.240
Never install copies passed around as files, such as GB WhatsApp. They are not made by WhatsApp, they can steal your messages, and WhatsApp can ban accounts that use them.

11
00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:10.500
If you have one, back up what you need, uninstall it, and install the official app.

12
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:23.350
Two-step verification adds a six-digit PIN that you create. Then anyone trying to register your number on a new phone needs the SMS code and your PIN.

13
00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:28.120
Step one. Open Settings, then Account, then Two-step verification.

14
00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:41.380
Step two. Tap Turn on and type a six-digit PIN you will remember. Do not use your birthday, 123456, or your ATM PIN.

15
00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.080
Step three. Type it again to confirm.

16
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:53.710
Step four. Add an email address you can open. WhatsApp uses it to send you a reset link if you forget the PIN.

17
00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:59.640
Step five. Write the PIN somewhere safe at home, not in your phone notes.

18
00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:08.140
And remember the rule. Your SMS code is like your ATM PIN. WhatsApp will never call or message you to ask for it.

19
00:02:09.390 --> 00:02:17.040
Here is how the trick works. Chioma in Owerri sells hair products. One evening a message comes from her cousin's account.

20
00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:21.550
It says, I mistakenly sent my code to your number, please send it to me.

21
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:36.590
At the same moment, an SMS with a six-digit code arrives. Chioma recognises the pattern. Someone is trying to register her number on another phone, and her cousin's account has probably already been hijacked.

22
00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:44.580
She does not send the code. She calls her cousin on a normal phone call, and the cousin says she sent no message.

23
00:02:45.830 --> 00:02:52.500
Then Chioma turns on two-step verification with a new PIN and her email. Her account stays safe.

24
00:02:53.750 --> 00:03:02.990
Now open Settings, Privacy. My contacts means people saved in your phone. For last seen and online, choose My contacts or Nobody.

25
00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.700
Set your profile photo to My contacts, and avoid photos of your children.

26
00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:14.600
Set your status to My contacts, so strangers do not follow your daily life.

27
00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:27.240
This one matters most. Set Groups to My contacts. It stops strangers adding you to investment, crypto or forex trading groups, one of the most common ways scams begin.

28
00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:37.010
If you get spam calls, switch on Silence unknown callers. Calls from unsaved numbers then go to your call list without ringing.

29
00:03:38.260 --> 00:03:45.870
Your messages live on your phone, not on WhatsApp's servers. If the phone is stolen and you have no backup, the chats are gone.

30
00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:48.530
Open Settings, Chats, Chat backup.

31
00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:54.850
On Android, link your Google account. On iPhone, the backup goes to iCloud.

32
00:03:56.100 --> 00:04:02.930
Set the frequency to daily or weekly. Videos make the backup large, so decide whether to include them.

33
00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:08.190
Many people back up only on Wi-Fi, to save their data bundle.

34
00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:22.840
Tap Back up now, and check the screen shows the time as just now. When Bisi in Ibadan moved to a new phone, she signed in to the same Google account and tapped Restore. Her customers' chats all came back.

35
00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:38.270
To remember. Install only the official app. Never share the six-digit code or your PIN. Turn on two-step verification with your email. Set Groups to My contacts. And switch on backup before you need it.

36
00:04:39.520 --> 00:04:49.190
Now pick up your phone. Check your app is official and updated, run Privacy checkup, turn on two-step verification, and run one backup on Wi-Fi.

37
00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:56.770
Take a screenshot showing two-step verification is on, without the PIN, and continue with the lessons below.
